IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 7 -- Offences relating to the armed forces`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 131, 132, 133, 134, 135, 136, 137, 138, 139, 140, 140A, 140B.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- Twelve sections about civilians and the forces. Every offence but s 140 relates to
-- "an officer or any serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces
-- lawfully present in Singapore", and s 140B extends the whole Chapter, with the
-- necessary modifications, to members of the Singapore Police Force and its volunteer,
-- auxiliary and special forces. That reach is one rule, `the person concerned is
-- within Chapter 7`, conjoined by every section that names the officer or serviceman.
--
-- The pairs ss 131/132, 133/134 and the single s 138 are abetments of mutiny,
-- assault on a superior and insubordination, the second of each pair being the case
-- where the thing abetted is committed in consequence. s 131 also reaches an attempt
-- to seduce from allegiance or duty, which needs no abetment. s 135 abets desertion;
-- s 136 harbours a deserter (with s 140A's meaning of "harbour"); s 137 is the
-- ship's master on whose vessel a deserter is concealed. s 140 is the civilian in a
-- serviceman's dress.
--
-- The abetments here are facts on the record, not the s 107 Abetment record: the
-- section names what is abetted and makes the abetment a principal offence, as
-- ss 121 and 489E do.
--
-- s 139 is a saving: where service discipline law punishes a corresponding offence, a
-- person subject to that law is not punishable under this Code for it. It removes the
-- Code offence for that person, so it is a negated conjunct on every wrapper.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED.

§§ `Section 140B -- The person concerned`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 140B"
GIVEN af IS AN `Armed Forces Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person concerned is within Chapter 7` IF
        af's `the person concerned is an officer or serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore`
    OR  af's `the person concerned is a member of the Singapore Police Force or of a volunteer auxiliary or special force attached to or under the jurisdiction of that Force`

§§ `Sections 131 and 132 -- Mutiny, and seduction from duty`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 131"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes abetting mutiny or attempting to seduce an officer or serviceman from his duty under Penal Code 1871 section 131
GIVEN af IS AN `Armed Forces Offence` @desc Abetting the committing of mutiny by an officer or serviceman of the Singapore Armed Forces, a visiting force or (s 140B) the police, or attempting to seduce one from his allegiance or duty.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes abetting mutiny or seducing from duty` IF
        `the person concerned is within Chapter 7` af
    AND (   af's `abets the committing of mutiny by the officer or serviceman`
         OR af's `attempts to seduce the officer or serviceman from his allegiance or his duty`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 132"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes abetting mutiny where mutiny is committed in consequence under Penal Code 1871 section 132
GIVEN af IS AN `Armed Forces Offence` @desc Abetting mutiny by an officer or serviceman, where mutiny is committed in consequence of the abetment.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes abetting a mutiny that is committed` IF
        `the person concerned is within Chapter 7` af
    AND af's `abets the committing of mutiny by the officer or serviceman`
    AND af's `mutiny is committed in consequence of the abetment`

§§ `Sections 133 and 134 -- Assault on a superior officer`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 133"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes abetting an assault by an officer or serviceman on a superior officer under Penal Code 1871 section 133
GIVEN af IS AN `Armed Forces Offence` @desc Abetting an assault by an officer or serviceman on a superior officer in the execution of his office.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes abetting an assault on a superior officer` IF
        `the person concerned is within Chapter 7` af
    AND af's `abets an assault by the officer or serviceman on a superior officer being in the execution of his office`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 134"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes abetting an assault on a superior officer where the assault is committed under Penal Code 1871 section 134
GIVEN af IS AN `Armed Forces Offence` @desc Abetting such an assault, where the assault is committed in consequence of the abetment.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes abetting an assault on a superior officer that is committed` IF
        `constitutes abetting an assault on a superior officer` af
    AND af's `the assault is committed in consequence of the abetment`

§§ `Sections 135 to 137 -- Desertion`

-- s 136 harbouring takes the s 140A meaning. s 137 is a negligence offence on the
-- master or person in charge of a merchant vessel: liable "though ignorant of such
-- concealment" if he might have known of it but for some neglect of his duty or want
-- of discipline on board. No knowledge is required, so none is conjoined.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 135"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes abetting the desertion of an officer or serviceman under Penal Code 1871 section 135
GIVEN af IS AN `Armed Forces Offence` @desc Abetting the desertion of an officer or serviceman.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes abetting desertion` IF
        `the person concerned is within Chapter 7` af
    AND af's `abets the desertion of the officer or serviceman`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 140A"
GIVEN af IS AN `Armed Forces Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person harbours the deserter within section 140A` IF
        af's `harbours the officer or serviceman`
    OR  af's `supplies the person with shelter food drink money clothes arms ammunition or means of conveyance or assists the person in any way to evade apprehension`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 136"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes harbouring a deserter under Penal Code 1871 section 136
GIVEN af IS AN `Armed Forces Offence` @desc Knowing or having reason to believe that an officer or serviceman has deserted, harbouring him (in the s 140A sense) with the intention of preventing his apprehension.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes harbouring a deserter` IF
        `the person concerned is within Chapter 7` af
    AND af's `knows or has reason to believe that the officer or serviceman has deserted`
    AND `the person harbours the deserter within section 140A` af
    AND af's `intends to prevent the officer or serviceman from being apprehended`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 137"
@export Decide whether the master of a merchant vessel is liable for a deserter concealed on board through his negligence under Penal Code 1871 section 137
GIVEN af IS AN `Armed Forces Offence` @desc The master or person in charge of a merchant vessel on which a deserter is concealed, who might have known of the concealment but for some neglect of duty or want of discipline on board. Ignorance of the concealment is no answer.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes negligently carrying a concealed deserter` IF
        `the person concerned is within Chapter 7` af
    AND af's `is the master or person in charge of a merchant vessel on board which a deserter from the forces is concealed`
    AND af's `might have known of the concealment but for some neglect of his duty as master or person in charge or but for some want of discipline on board the vessel`

§§ `Section 138 -- Insubordination`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 138"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes abetting an act of insubordination by an officer or serviceman under Penal Code 1871 section 138
GIVEN af IS AN `Armed Forces Offence` @desc Abetting what the person knows to be an act of insubordination by an officer or serviceman, where the act is committed in consequence of the abetment.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes abetting insubordination` IF
        `the person concerned is within Chapter 7` af
    AND af's `abets what he knows to be an act of insubordination by the officer or serviceman`
    AND af's `the act of insubordination is committed in consequence of the abetment`

§§ `Section 140 -- Wearing the dress of a serviceman`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 140"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes wearing the dress or carrying the token of a serviceman under Penal Code 1871 section 140
GIVEN af IS AN `Armed Forces Offence` @desc A person who is not a serviceman wearing garb or carrying a token resembling a serviceman's, intending that it may be believed that he is one.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes wearing the dress of a serviceman` IF
        af's `is not a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore`
    AND af's `wears any garb or carries any token resembling any garb or token used by such a serviceman`
    AND af's `intends that it may be believed that he is such a serviceman`

§§ `Section 139 -- Saving`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 139"
GIVEN af IS AN `Armed Forces Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is subject to service discipline law for a corresponding offence` IF
    af's `provision is made in a law relating to the discipline of the Singapore Armed Forces for the punishment of a corresponding offence and the person is subject to that provision`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes an armed forces offence` IF
        (   `constitutes abetting mutiny or seducing from duty` (a's `armed forces offence`)
         OR `constitutes abetting a mutiny that is committed` (a's `armed forces offence`)
         OR `constitutes abetting an assault on a superior officer` (a's `armed forces offence`)
         OR `constitutes abetting an assault on a superior officer that is committed` (a's `armed forces offence`)
         OR `constitutes abetting desertion` (a's `armed forces offence`)
         OR `constitutes harbouring a deserter` (a's `armed forces offence`)
         OR `constitutes negligently carrying a concealed deserter` (a's `armed forces offence`)
         OR `constitutes abetting insubordination` (a's `armed forces offence`)
         OR `constitutes wearing the dress of a serviceman` (a's `armed forces offence`))
    AND NOT (`the person is subject to service discipline law for a corresponding offence` (a's `armed forces offence`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
